## 3. Extractors that embody the changed behavior

### 3.1. `AuthUser` extractor

```rust
pub struct AuthUser {
    pub user_id: Uuid,
}

#[async_trait]
impl FromRequest for AuthUser {
    type Rejection = Error;

    async fn from_request(req: &mut RequestParts<Body>) -> Result<Self, Self::Rejection> {
        let ctx: Extension<ApiContext> = Extension::from_request(req)
            .await
            .expect("BUG: ApiContext was not added as an extension");

        let auth_header = req
            .headers()
            .ok_or(Error::Unauthorized)?
            .get(AUTHORIZATION)
            .ok_or(Error::Unauthorized)?;

        Self::from_authorization(&ctx, auth_header)
    }
}
```

`from_request` delegates to:

```rust
impl AuthUser {
    /// Attempt to parse `Self` from an `Authorization` header.
    fn from_authorization(ctx: &ApiContext, auth_header: &HeaderValue) -> Result<Self, Error> {
        // ... parse & verify JWT ...
        let (_header, claims) = jwt.into();

        if claims.exp + GRACE_PERIOD_SECONDS < OffsetDateTime::now_utc().unix_timestamp() {
            log::debug!("token expired");
            return Err(Error::Unauthorized);
        }

        Ok(Self {
            user_id: claims.user_id,
        })
    }
}
```

Evidence: `src/http/extractor.rs`.

**Conclusion:** Any handler that takes `AuthUser` as an argument now perceives tokens within 300 seconds after `exp` as valid, whereas before they would have been rejected immediately.

### 3.2. `MaybeAuthUser` extractor

```rust
pub struct MaybeAuthUser(pub Option<AuthUser>);

#[async_trait]
impl FromRequest for MaybeAuthUser {
    type Rejection = Error;

    async fn from_request(req: &mut RequestParts<Body>) -> Result<Self, Self::Rejection> {
        let ctx: Extension<ApiContext> = Extension::from_request(req)
            .await
            .expect("BUG: ApiContext was not added as an extension");

        Ok(Self(
            req.headers()
                .and_then(|headers| {
                    let auth_header = headers.get(AUTHORIZATION)?;
                    Some(AuthUser::from_authorization(&ctx, auth_header))
                })
                .transpose()?,
        ))
    }
}
```

Evidence: `src/http/extractor.rs`.

`MaybeAuthUser` still reuses `AuthUser::from_authorization`, so the same grace period applies when an optional auth context is present.

